    "Counts are derived with the standard library only: xml.etree for the forms, a text pass for the Python call sites. No Qt, no display.",
    "The class inventory, per-file widget counts and the 72 distinct (class, member) pairs match qt-strategy.md \u00a72.3\u2013\u00a72.4.",
    "'accesses' pins every textual access this tool finds; it is not \u00a72.4's 'Calls' column, which uses a different counting rule.",
    "Method-vs-signal is inferred from a trailing .connect, a heuristic; the signal payloads and connection counts need the panels to run and are not pinned.",
    "Not reproducible without Qt: widget construction, signal payloads, alias-based access (none was found in these modules), and \u00a72.4's '7 signals / 34 connections' aggregate for the six core panels.",
    "The checkout's git revision is not verified; counts are the drift check. Declared revision: 33adf61."
